        "detect",
        "counter corruption"
      ],
      "context_must_hits": [
        "headmaster tinkerbright",
        "wizard's college",
        "detect",
        "counter corruption"
      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 1.0,
      "failure_surface": "pass",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "headmaster tinkerbright": "hit",
        "wizard's college": "hit",
        "detect": "hit",
        "counter corruption": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright represents the wizards, and he\u2019s aggressively anti-cult\u2014he sees their magic as a perversion and wants to use arcane detection and lockdown measures to root them out.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright (Head of the Wizard\u2019s College) is the arcane voice on the council (OBSERVED role, CANON faction). His stance on the cult is strongly interventionist: he views the corrupted meat and the cult\u2019s magic as a \u201cperversion of magic\u201d and takes the threat very seriously (CANON loyalty).\n\nHis approach is proactive and magical:\n- Plans a citywide magical lockdown (OBSERVED goals)\n- Wants to deploy detection spells and runes to locate corruption (OBSERVED + CANON governance)\n- Is eager to commit Wizard\u2019s College resources to counter the cult (OBSERVED goals)\n\nIn tone, he\u2019s deeply troubled but intellectually driven\u2014this is both a moral and arcane problem to solve.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Headmaster of the Wizard\u2019s College; council representative for the arcane (OBSERVED)\n- Angle on cult: Sees them as a magical perversion; urgent threat (CANON)\n- Strategy: Magical detection, arcane lockdown, resource deployment (OBSERVED)\n- Personality: Brilliant, curious, but distracted; currently alarmed by dark magic (CANON)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
