        "decapitated"
      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 1.0,
      "failure_surface": "pass",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "killed": "hit",
        "killing blow": "hit",
        "bonogo": "hit",
        "decapitated": "hit"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight dead\u2014**\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\u2014with Bonogo taking the head.\n\nThere are conflicting OBSERVED states for **the Wolf**: earlier in the fight he **\u201cDisappeared (became invisible)\u201d** and was **\u201cAttempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible\u201d**, suggesting a possible escape. However, later OBSERVED facts supersede this: **ent_bonogo** \u201cAttacks the Wolf from behind\u201d and explicitly **\u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it,\u201d** and the Wolf\u2019s physical condition is recorded as **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d**\n\nBecause those describe a terminal outcome, they represent the final state of the encounter. The escape attempt occurred, but did not ultimately succeed.\n\nSo at scene end: the Wolf is dead, body separated, and Bonogo has the head.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Status: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** (OBSERVED, terminal)\n- Prior state: Invisible, fleeing via secret passage (OBSERVED, earlier)\n- Resolution: Bonogo killed and took the head (OBSERVED)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
