      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no evidence Thalia is corrupted like the guards; what we have suggests something different\u2014she\u2019s acting under The Wolf\u2019s influence or orders, not confirmed corruption.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Corruption marker (Guards): \u201cAll checked guards have an oily sheen to their eyes.\u201d (OBSERVED)\n- Thalia behavior: \u201cThe Wolf orders Thalia to attack the group.\u201d (OBSERVED)\n- The Wolf influence: Positioned \u201cat Thalia\u2019s shoulder\u201d and actively directing actions (OBSERVED)\n\nBased on the projection, the guards\u2019 corruption is explicitly tied to physical signs (the \u201coily sheen to their eyes\u201d). There is no such indicator given for Thalia. Instead, her involvement in the fight is directly linked to The Wolf issuing commands and his proximity/control.\n\nSo, current state: Thalia is not confirmed corrupted like the guards. The available facts support that her actions stem from The Wolf\u2019s influence (possibly coercion, manipulation, or command), which is distinct from the established guard corruption.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
