      "answer": "TL;DR: The council room itself fights back with **arcane traps, illusion effects, and environmental hazards**\u2014especially targeting anyone without amulets\u2014causing paralysis, force damage, disorientation, and falling debris.\n\nHere\u2019s what actively screws with the fight:\n\n- **Arcane trap bursts (CANON/OBSERVED)**: These can **temporarily paralyze** players and deal **2d6 force damage**. Per CANON, they specifically target those **without amulets**, while **Guards** are exempt due to their amulets.\n- **Illusions (CANON)**: The room uses **illusory walls/illusion spells**, leaving players **disoriented** and already noted as being thrown off by similar effects.\n- **Environmental hazards (OBSERVED)**: The fight space includes **falling debris hazards**, forcing movement and dodging under pressure.\n- **Rune alarms (OBSERVED)**: These trigger reinforcements and escalate the fight dynamically.\n- **Sensory interference (CANON)**: The **constant hum of wall-embedded gears** shifts\u2014players may notice changes in the hum signaling something dangerous or imminent.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps targeting non-amulet wearers; guards immune via amulets\n- Terrain: Unstable (falling debris)\n- Magical Effects: Illusions causing disorientation; paralysis + force damage traps\n- Alerts: Rune alarms triggering reinforcements\n- Atmosphere: Mechanical hum that subtly telegraphs changes",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
