      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s not enough direct evidence to confirm Thalia is untrustworthy, but something may be off\u2014she\u2019s been involved in tense or ambiguous situations.\n\nFrom the available OBSERVED facts:\n- **Caelynn** trusted Thalia enough to **instruct her to bring a potion to Lesandra at the Wizard\u2019s College**, suggesting at least baseline confidence in her reliability.\n- However, **Stafl attacks Thalia after being revived**, which signals either suspicion, confusion, or a perceived threat involving her (the cause is not specified).\n\nNo explicit facts describe Thalia\u2019s motives, mental state, or allegiance, so any judgment about deception or corruption would be speculative.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Relationships:\n  - Trusted by **Caelynn** for task delegation (OBSERVED)\n  - Targeted by **Stafl** in a sudden attack (OBSERVED)\n- Role in current events:\n  - Acting as a messenger or agent in crisis response (OBSERVED)\n\nConclusion: Thalia hasn\u2019t been proven untrustworthy, but her involvement in a sudden intra-party attack and the broader unstable situation (corruption, paranoia among guards, citywide threat) means caution is warranted.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
