      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The cult advances unopposed\u2014using hidden routes and council influence\u2014to sabotage defenses and push their summoning, while the city slides closer to disaster with unrest and potential lockdown fallout.\n\nIf the council stalls, the immediate risk is momentum: **the cult (group)** is already active in-town and \u201cbelieved to be using hidden city infrastructure,\u201d with goals to \u201caccess the heart of the city\u201d and \u201ccomplete their summoning.\u201d Delay gives them time to pivot\u2014\u201cuse alternative routes if primary routes are blocked\u201d and potentially \u201csabotage or corrupt the cauldrons.\u201d\n\nCompounding that, **CANON** states \u201ccult members have influence in the council,\u201d so inaction may not be neutral\u2014it can actively favor the cult\u2019s strategy.\n\nAt the city level, **OBSERVED** status says it\u2019s \u201cbrought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate,\u201d with a \u201cplanned magical lockdown\u201d that could isolate districts if triggered late. Meanwhile, unrest from the toll and protests continues to destabilize things.\n\nFor the **Players (group)**, they are already \u201cdelayed by lengthy deliberation,\u201d risking missed windows on warehouses, the Wolf intel, and coordinated responses.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Weak points; integrity concerns; proposed lockdown (CANON/OBSERVED)\n- Geography: Hidden passages/sewers enable cult movement (CANON)\n- Governance: Council indecision; cult influence \u092d\u0940\u0924\u0930 (OBSERVED/CANON)\n- Economy: Festival-critical; disruption likely if crisis escalates (CANON)\n- Operational Status: Active cult ops; city trending toward disaster (OBSERVED)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
