      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room is tense and chaotic after the fight\u2014guards shaken, signs of illusion and corruption linger, and the Wolf\u2019s **decapitated; head removed from body;** state makes the threat unmistakably real.\n\nWhat stands out:\n\n- The Wolf\u2019s body is the focal point. His **decapitated; head removed from body;** condition confirms the fight\u2019s finality, and his corpse may still show the **oily sheen to his eyes**, reinforcing the corruption angle (OBSERVED).\n- Guards are positioned in a ring along the walls, visibly tense and unsettled (OBSERVED). Some may also show that same **oily sheen to their eyes**, hinting the problem isn\u2019t isolated.\n- The aftermath of illusion magic lingers\u2014scorch marks, displaced objects, or confusion about where the \u201creal\u201d fight happened, consistent with his use of duplicates (CANON + OBSERVED).\n- Subtle environmental cues matter: footsteps echoing in halls or a change in the city\u2019s ambient hum can signal something still unfolding nearby (CANON).\n- The chamber feels politically charged\u2014this is not just a battlefield, but a place where the players\u2019 account will immediately shape council decisions (OBSERVED).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Illusion use (Wolf duplicates)\n- NPC State: Guards tense; some corrupted (oily eyes)\n- Notable Event: **decapitated; head removed from body;**\n- Atmosphere: Confusion, tension, political weight immediately following combat",
