      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Chambers got blasted by a Fireball, triggering its magical defenses, and ended the session in a disheveled state with active wards and illusions altering the space.\n\nDuring Session 12 (OBSERVED), several clear changes/damages occurred in the **Council Chambers**:\n- A major destructive event: **\u201calmost the entire room is lit up by Fireball\u201d**, indicating widespread blast impact across the chamber.\n- The room\u2019s defenses reacted: **runes along the walls activated when Caelynn cast her spell**, bringing ancient wards online.\n- Environmental shifts: **Illusory Walls** became active, changing how the space could be navigated and perceived.\n- Overall condition: the chamber is explicitly noted as **Disheveled**, reflecting the aftermath of the magical chaos.\n\nThese changes override the room\u2019s normal CANON state as a pristine, orderly council space\u2014Session 12 leaves it magically active and physically disturbed.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition: Disheveled (OBSERVED)\n- Defenses: Activated runes, ancient wards, Illusory Walls (OBSERVED)\n- Atmosphere: Dominated by Fireball blast and heightened magical activity (OBSERVED)\n- Geography: Core structure unchanged (large circular room, central table), but traversal impacted by illusions (OBSERVED)",
