      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead \u2014 **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** \u2014 and cannot currently act; he previously showed signs of corruption (\u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d).\n\nThe **OBSERVED physical_condition** includes the terminal outcomes **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**, which overrides earlier escape/invisibility states. Although he was at one point **\u201cAttempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible\u201d** and listed as having **\u201cescapes\u201d**, those are superseded by the later lethal outcome.\n\nCorruption status: prior to death, the Wolf had **\u201can oily sheen to his eyes\u201d**, indicating active corruption influence. There is no evidence in the projection that this corruption was removed before death.\n\nBonogo\u2019s role reinforces this final state: **\u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it.\u201d**\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition (OBSERVED): **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d; \u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d**\n- Operational Status (OBSERVED): Escape attempts earlier, but no longer applicable due to death\n- Faction (OBSERVED): Cultist\n- Mental State (OBSERVED): Desperate, regretful, begging for release prior to death\n\nCurrent state at end of Session 12: dead, formerly corrupted, no indication of purification.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
