      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive saboteur manipulating events and trying to escape; after, he is **Decapitated; head removed from body**, no longer an active threat and likely only useful for Speak with Dead.\n\nBefore the fight (OBSERVED + CANON):\n- The Wolf is a **second-in-command guard** and **cultist/sympathizer** actively sabotaging the council.\n- Uses **illusory duplicates** (CANON) to confuse enemies and control the battlefield.\n- Behavior: deceptive, strategic, attempting to **mislead the council** and **escape via invisibility and secret tunnels**.\n- Mental state: **desperate, regretful, begging for release or death**, but still acting with agency.\n- Operational status: **actively fleeing, fighting, and manipulating** events.\n\nAfter the fight (OBSERVED):\n- Physical condition: **Decapitated; head removed from body** (terminal outcome).\n- Operational status: no longer escaping or acting\u2014his plans are halted.\n- Narrative shift: from **active antagonist** to **information source** (players plan Speak with Dead).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Saboteur \u2192 Corpse / interrogation target  \n- Physical Condition: Active combatant \u2192 **Decapitated; head removed from body**  \n- Tactics: Illusions, deception, escape \u2192 none  \n- Narrative Function: Threat \u2192 clue source",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
